"""Think-SFT (trained with no reward) passes 381 of 538 code problems once the grader reads its answer format: 10.8 points
above Base + cue (323) and 3.7 below RL (401). As first graded it passed 301, below Base + cue (317).

The page of one finding, served at /finding/no-reward-on-code (view.py serves every tools/finding_<slug>.py) and reached
from its tile on /findings, which ICON draws. The picture is one lit plate with three rows of 538 marks, one mark per code
problem: Base + cue, Think-SFT + cue and RL (top to bottom). Each row is sorted by outcome, so it reads as a bar: the
programs that passed the tests (blue) on the left, the programs the first rule did not read as written (red) in the
middle, the failed ones (faint) on the right. The one control, "How the grader reads the answer", has two positions: the
first rule (the last fenced ```python block) and the second rule (also a program after a line `python` with no opening
fence, without the lines that are only CODE, the placeholder copied from the prompt). On the switch each red mark travels
into the passed or the failed part of its row and the counts run with the marks: Think-SFT 301 -> 381, Base + cue 317 -> 323,
RL 401 -> 401. A click on a mark (or Enter on the picture) shows that problem, the three answers' outcomes under both rules
and the stored end of each answer, with the missing fence or the copied CODE line marked.

Address: /finding/no-reward-on-code#[first/][<panel> or <HumanEval-1 | Mbpp-2>]. The second rule is the default and is left
out. An empty address opens on the first rule and plays the change once, then rests on the second rule; with reduced motion it
shows the second rule at once. The rules are in .claude/skills/finding-page/SKILL.md; the looks are those of
tools/architecture.py (.claude/skills/site-ui/SKILL.md). The finding is board item result-f698c2 (first grading
result-9d38d9; result-b847a0 on the unread answers).

The artifacts are on branch audit (main was frozen), copied at commit fa46a00: the regrade readouts
studies/rlneurons/results/code_think/regrade_v3-01/ and regrade_v2-01/ (commit f4b1f47), the first readout
results/code_think/readout.json and the README section 'Regrade with two more extraction rules'. The per-problem rows are the
regrade job's output runs/ih-1115-224033-da9c/<cell>/answers_v3.jsonl, which is not in git; PROBLEMS below is copied from them,
and running this file checks it against the committed readouts (counts, reruns, the paired intervals recomputed with the
readout's own bootstrap) and, when the rows are present, against the rows.

    uv run --no-project --with numpy python tools/finding_no_reward_on_code.py [--runs <folder holding ih-1115-224033-da9c>]
        checks DATA, LINE and PROBLEMS; the row comparison is skipped, and says so, when the rows are not there
    ... python tools/finding_no_reward_on_code.py --runs <folder> --write    rewrites PROBLEMS from the rows
"""
