    ["Mbpp/455", "Write a function to check whether the given month number contains 31 days or not.\nYour code should pass this test:\nassert check_monthnumb_number(5)==True", ["ff", 768, 0, "NameError: name 'check_monthnumb_number' is not defined. Did you mean: 'check_month_number'?", "", "that list. The test case uses assert to check that check_month_number(5) returns True, which it does. And any other month (like 2, 6, etc.) would return False. So this should be correct.```python\ndef check_month_number(month_num):\n    return month_num in [1, 3, 5, 7, 8, 10, 12]\n\nassert check_month_number(5) == True\n```"], ["pp", 983, 0, "", "", "\n```python\ndef check_monthnumb_number(month):\n    return month in {1, 3, 5, 7, 8, 10, 12}\n``` \n\nThat's three backticks, then python, then the code, then three backticks again.\n\nTherefore the final answer is as above.\n</think>\n\n```\npython\ndef check_monthnumb_number(month):\n    return month in {1, 3, 5, 7, 8, 10, 12}\n```"], ["ff", 1419, 0, "NameError: name 'check_monthnumb_number' is not defined. Did you mean: 'check_month_number'?", "", "Although the problem assumes valid month numbers between 1 and 12, the function will still work correctly even if provided with invalid inputs (though such cases are not covered in the problem statement).\n\nThis approach efficiently checks the validity and membership, ensuring the solution is both concise and effective."]],
